WEBVTT

00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:04.380
<i>These words were written 
in a book I once read:</i>

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:09.980
<i>"A person's fate is in a constant 
state of fluctuation and change."</i>

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:28.220
...st go back...

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:31.260
Must return to ...ames.

00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:47.890
...have to hurry...

00:00:47.890 --> 00:00:50.150
Hitaki, I'm sorry.

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:54.650
I've secured the Japanese-style book.

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:57.320
All right, mission complete.

00:00:57.320 --> 00:00:58.990
A-Are you going to kill me?!

00:00:58.990 --> 00:01:00.660
Like we'd do that.

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:05.450
I was just carrying the book like 
I was asked! P-Please, spare me!

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:09.800
We're the Imperial Library Intelligence 
Asset Management Bureau.

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:12.550
Pleasure to make your acquaintance.

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:27.090
Hitaki!

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:32.580
<i>At the time, I wasn't even remotely aware</i>

00:01:33.650 --> 00:01:40.400
<i>of how greatly this horrible incident 
would tilt the scales of my fate.</i>

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:16.960
The Glow of the Cursed Tome

00:03:14.610 --> 00:03:16.960
-Aura-

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:20.470
Nee-san!

00:03:20.790 --> 00:03:23.220
Is it true that you're getting married?

00:03:24.080 --> 00:03:25.100
Hitaki...

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:26.610
What is the meaning of this?

00:03:26.610 --> 00:03:28.460
I didn't hear anything about it!

00:03:28.460 --> 00:03:29.560
It's not fair.

00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:31.730
Why am I the only one you didn't tell?!

00:03:33.220 --> 00:03:34.970
I'd planned to tell you soon...

00:03:34.970 --> 00:03:36.030
Why?!

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:40.110
Is it for money?

00:03:41.480 --> 00:03:43.190
It is, isn't it?

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:46.620
Father's selling you off!

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:51.370
He wants to protect the family by selling 
you to some useless nouveau riche!

00:03:51.370 --> 00:03:52.780
Hitaki...

00:03:52.780 --> 00:03:54.000
No, that's not what it is!

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.540
Of course it is!

00:03:55.540 --> 00:03:58.040
Don't you have any pride as a noble?!

00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:02.480
Refuse. Refuse it immediately!

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:05.240
I understand.

00:04:05.240 --> 00:04:08.300
You don't really want to 
do this either, do you?

00:04:09.010 --> 00:04:10.520
That's not true!

00:04:12.570 --> 00:04:14.650
This is none of your business!

00:04:21.390 --> 00:04:22.660
I really...

00:04:23.600 --> 00:04:25.780
I really hate you!

00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:27.670
Hitaki!

00:04:32.340 --> 00:04:33.540
Hitaki...

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:35.870
Tsugumi-sama.

00:04:37.240 --> 00:04:38.350
Gramps...

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:43.820
Isn't it awful? He's such a selfish boy.

00:04:43.820 --> 00:04:48.430
Hitaki-sama overheard the servants gossiping.

00:04:51.280 --> 00:04:53.430
Have they settled on Tsugumi-sama's marriage?

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:55.270
I heard it's with the Yashiro family.

00:04:55.270 --> 00:04:58.380
They say that the other 
party readily agreed to it.

00:04:58.380 --> 00:05:01.030
I feel terrible for Tsugumi-sama, though.

00:05:01.030 --> 00:05:04.320
True, but with the way things are
for the Kuze family right now...

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:05.460
Hey, you two!

00:05:06.690 --> 00:05:07.980
Hitaki-sama?

00:05:07.980 --> 00:05:11.280
Tell me everything about
what you're discussing.

00:05:12.010 --> 00:05:13.860
I am very sorry.

00:05:13.860 --> 00:05:17.260
This was my failing as the 
steward of the Kuze household.

00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:21.090
No, it's not your fault at all.

00:05:21.670 --> 00:05:23.210
It's mine.

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:26.510
I've spoiled him too much.

00:05:26.510 --> 00:05:28.220
No, not at all.

00:05:28.660 --> 00:05:30.870
Tsugumi-sama... you, ah...

00:05:30.870 --> 00:05:32.560
I'm fine.

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:34.860
I've known since I was a child

00:05:34.860 --> 00:05:36.590
that I would one day marry the man

00:05:36.590 --> 00:05:40.680
my father chose for me, as a 
daughter of the Kuze family.

00:05:41.460 --> 00:05:44.300
It's just come a bit sooner than I expected.

00:05:45.010 --> 00:05:48.360
The other party is a respectable
family that has made a fortune

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:51.090
in maritime shipping, despite
being of common origin.

00:05:51.090 --> 00:05:54.240
Mr. Yashiro, the head of the family,
is a very kind man.

00:05:54.880 --> 00:05:57.820
His son will be a good match for you.

00:05:57.820 --> 00:05:59.640
Yes, Father.

00:06:02.280 --> 00:06:04.250
I had many friends at the girls' school

00:06:04.250 --> 00:06:07.710
who got married at the 
same time they graduated.

00:06:07.710 --> 00:06:10.740
Some of them had been 
engaged since they were born.

00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:15.270
So I'll be fine.

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:16.990
Tsugumi-sama...

00:06:16.990 --> 00:06:19.270
Gramps, please ready the car.

00:06:20.360 --> 00:06:22.860
I'm going to go to town as planned.

00:06:22.860 --> 00:06:24.780
But what about Hitaki-sama?

00:06:25.010 --> 00:06:27.620
I'll still go even if he won't.

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:30.160
I'm going to buy him something he likes.

00:06:30.890 --> 00:06:33.260
What a lovely idea.

00:06:33.260 --> 00:06:36.910
That's why I need you to have 
the pancakes ready as usual.

00:06:37.640 --> 00:06:40.290
Yes, of course.

00:06:52.050 --> 00:06:57.810
<i>The Kuze family was already in 
economic decline when I was young.</i>

00:06:58.700 --> 00:07:01.160
<i>My mother, who was always physically weak,</i>

00:07:01.160 --> 00:07:03.880
<i>returned to her family's home to convalesce.</i>

00:07:04.750 --> 00:07:08.440
<i>And so it was just the 
two of us, Hitaki and me.</i>

00:07:09.260 --> 00:07:13.960
<i>My father established his business, 
and it was doing well enough.</i>

00:07:14.350 --> 00:07:19.270
<i>But it was dealt a hard blow by the great 
imperial city earthquake and couldn't recover.</i>

00:07:22.340 --> 00:07:26.460
<i>If I marry into the Yashiro family, 
my father will receive a loan.</i>

00:07:27.260 --> 00:07:28.860
<i>It's the only way.</i>

00:07:28.860 --> 00:07:32.370
<i>It's the only way to save the Kuze family.</i>

00:07:33.470 --> 00:07:36.470
Shiseido Bookstore

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:38.150
Welcome.

00:07:38.150 --> 00:07:39.480
I'd like these.

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:41.480
Birdcage in the Summer Haze
Migiwa Shizuru

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:41.480
<b>Girls' World</b>

00:07:40.800 --> 00:07:43.020
Migiwa Shizuru?

00:07:43.020 --> 00:07:43.980
Yeah!

00:07:43.980 --> 00:07:46.360
Blazing Coffin

00:07:43.980 --> 00:07:47.050
I'm a huge fan of Migiwa-sensei.

00:07:49.820 --> 00:07:51.200
Eclairs

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:55.870
Ugetsudo

00:08:04.010 --> 00:08:07.380
<i>I'm sure Hitaki will calm down 
once he's had some tea.</i>

00:08:07.930 --> 00:08:09.790
<i>I'll tell him everything.</i>

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:12.670
<i>I won't keep secrets anymore.</i>

00:08:18.990 --> 00:08:21.290
Welcome home, Tsugumi-sama.

00:08:21.290 --> 00:08:22.770
Welcome home.

00:08:23.080 --> 00:08:24.540
I'm home.

00:08:24.540 --> 00:08:27.000
Gramps, please get the tea ready.

00:08:27.000 --> 00:08:27.770
Yes.

00:08:28.340 --> 00:08:32.150
I shall make Hitaki-sama's 
favorite Ceylon tea.

00:08:32.420 --> 00:08:33.340
Thank you.

00:08:41.230 --> 00:08:42.540
Hitaki.

00:08:44.810 --> 00:08:45.770
Wait!

00:08:46.300 --> 00:08:48.920
I bought you Migiwa 
Shizuru-sensei's new book!

00:08:48.920 --> 00:08:50.920
And eclairs from Ugetsudo!

00:09:01.430 --> 00:09:03.920
Birdcage in the Summer Haze
Migiwa Shizuru

00:09:01.980 --> 00:09:03.050
Hitaki...

00:09:06.220 --> 00:09:09.160
Tsugumi-sama, the tea is ready.

00:09:09.160 --> 00:09:10.120
Okay.

00:09:15.160 --> 00:09:16.450
Hitaki?

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:19.280
Come on, Hitaki.

00:09:19.280 --> 00:09:21.800
Gramps made pancakes.

00:09:21.800 --> 00:09:23.340
You must be hungry.

00:09:24.920 --> 00:09:26.830
I also have also eclairs from Ugetsudo,

00:09:26.830 --> 00:09:29.460
and I've brought you a book 
by Migiwa Shizuru-sensei.

00:09:30.460 --> 00:09:31.630
Hitaki...

00:09:32.790 --> 00:09:37.270
I'm sorry. It's all my fault for 
keeping secrets from you.

00:09:38.680 --> 00:09:41.400
Just let me talk to you, okay? Please!

00:09:46.110 --> 00:09:47.100
Hitaki...

00:09:48.140 --> 00:09:49.100
I'm coming in.

00:09:58.260 --> 00:09:59.600
Must go back...

00:10:00.620 --> 00:10:03.810
Must return... to the flames...

00:10:04.970 --> 00:10:06.750
What's that smell?

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:08.030
Oil?

00:10:10.560 --> 00:10:13.250
I must return... to the flames...

00:10:13.250 --> 00:10:14.470
Hitaki!

00:10:14.470 --> 00:10:15.760
Hitaki-sama!

00:10:24.010 --> 00:10:26.390
I have to return to...

00:10:26.890 --> 00:10:27.770
Hitaki-sama!

00:10:30.410 --> 00:10:32.320
Hitaki!

00:10:34.960 --> 00:10:38.360
<b>Imperial Capital University Hospital</b>

00:10:37.490 --> 00:10:41.370
Fortunately, if we can call it that, 
his life is not at risk.

00:10:42.600 --> 00:10:49.370
But for his burns to heal properly, 
he should have no visitors for the time being.

00:10:51.280 --> 00:10:54.960
It is such a relief that he's safe.

00:10:56.450 --> 00:10:57.880
Why...

00:10:59.350 --> 00:11:01.100
Why did he try to kill himself?

00:11:02.080 --> 00:11:04.240
I cannot believe it myself.

00:11:06.030 --> 00:11:07.740
It's my fault.

00:11:07.740 --> 00:11:11.650
No! It is not your fault 
at all, Tsugumi-sama!

00:11:11.880 --> 00:11:15.650
But he had no other reason to commit suicide!

00:11:15.650 --> 00:11:17.150
Tsugumi-sama!

00:11:17.150 --> 00:11:19.150
I know it's my fault.

00:11:19.760 --> 00:11:22.390
He even said he hated me...

00:11:22.390 --> 00:11:23.480
My lady!

00:11:24.160 --> 00:11:25.960
Please, pull yourself together.

00:11:25.960 --> 00:11:29.160
For Hitaki-sama's sake as well, 
you have to hold it together.

00:11:31.380 --> 00:11:33.960
But it has to be my fault.

00:11:33.960 --> 00:11:37.170
No, it was most likely not your fault.

00:11:46.260 --> 00:11:48.180
You are Kuze Tsugumi-san, correct?

00:11:49.140 --> 00:11:50.680
And you two are?

00:11:52.680 --> 00:11:54.120
Please forgive me.

00:11:55.810 --> 00:11:59.940
I am Ozaki Hayato from the Imperial Library 
Intelligence Asset Management Bureau.

00:12:00.380 --> 00:12:02.820
And I am Kougami Akira of the same.

00:12:03.800 --> 00:12:07.450
We have some questions we'd like 
to ask you about Kuze Hitaki-san.

00:12:07.730 --> 00:12:08.950
What?

00:12:09.580 --> 00:12:13.710
It may have been a book that 
nearly killed Hitaki-san.

00:12:16.290 --> 00:12:17.230
Huh?

00:12:24.110 --> 00:12:25.970
What do you mean when you say

00:12:26.340 --> 00:12:29.470
it was a book that nearly killed Hitaki-sama?

00:12:33.700 --> 00:12:37.040
Are you familiar with the term "cursed tomes"?

00:12:37.870 --> 00:12:39.420
Cursed tomes?

00:12:40.690 --> 00:12:42.790
You're really starting with that?

00:12:42.790 --> 00:12:45.430
I don't like beating around the bush.

00:12:45.980 --> 00:12:48.090
I guess that's true.

00:12:48.090 --> 00:12:49.120
Forgive me.

00:12:49.600 --> 00:12:53.750
"Cursed tome" refers to a book 
in which emotions reside.

00:12:54.110 --> 00:12:57.300
Emotions... in a book?

00:12:57.300 --> 00:12:58.000
Yes.

00:12:58.910 --> 00:13:03.130
More accurately, the emotions 
of whomever wrote it.

00:13:03.400 --> 00:13:05.720
At times, they can be very intense emotions.

00:13:09.260 --> 00:13:14.270
Cursed tomes are usually handwritten, 
Japanese-style books like this.

00:13:14.270 --> 00:13:17.270
This isn't a cursed tome, 
though. It's a normal book.

00:13:17.720 --> 00:13:21.640
These kinds of books can have an
effect on those who read them.

00:13:22.460 --> 00:13:24.280
They've existed for a long time,

00:13:24.900 --> 00:13:27.650
but with the rise of 
Western-style printed books,

00:13:27.660 --> 00:13:29.780
these incidents had all but stopped.

00:13:30.840 --> 00:13:32.040
But now...

00:13:32.270 --> 00:13:36.210
Recently, these incidents have 
been happening in succession.

00:13:37.380 --> 00:13:41.040
We believe that's what 
happened to your brother.

00:13:41.560 --> 00:13:42.820
To Hitaki?

00:13:43.400 --> 00:13:44.550
Another occurred today.

00:13:45.240 --> 00:13:47.430
Please keep this confidential.

00:13:47.430 --> 00:13:52.060
The son of the current Prime Minister, 
Ukai Shouzou, attempted suicide.

00:13:54.340 --> 00:13:57.040
It was proven to be due to a cursed tome.

00:13:58.160 --> 00:14:01.460
They both attempted suicide 
without any warning or reason,

00:14:01.460 --> 00:14:03.070
and they're close in age.

00:14:03.880 --> 00:14:07.110
We're here to find out if there 
might be some connection.

00:14:07.890 --> 00:14:12.080
Our primary function at the Imperial Library 
Intelligence Asset Management Bureau

00:14:12.530 --> 00:14:14.890
is finding and retrieving cursed tomes.

00:14:14.890 --> 00:14:17.620
There will be further damage 
if they aren't dealt with.

00:14:18.820 --> 00:14:20.890
Hitaki did that because of a book?

00:14:21.830 --> 00:14:25.090
Was there a book near him when it happened?

00:14:31.460 --> 00:14:33.220
There was! A Japanese-style one.

00:14:33.220 --> 00:14:34.730
Could you show it to us?

00:14:35.370 --> 00:14:37.480
I will bring it right away.

00:14:37.480 --> 00:14:38.540
Please do.

00:14:47.580 --> 00:14:49.170
Thank you for waiting.

00:14:58.730 --> 00:15:01.500
Gramps! Be careful! It's burning!

00:15:01.500 --> 00:15:03.010
It's on fire!

00:15:03.010 --> 00:15:03.720
Tsugumi-sama?

00:15:03.720 --> 00:15:06.720
Quick! Quick, put out the flames! Look out!

00:15:06.720 --> 00:15:08.010
Can you see something?

00:15:08.380 --> 00:15:09.520
What do you...

00:15:12.180 --> 00:15:13.460
You can't see it?

00:15:15.090 --> 00:15:16.510
They've been known to exist.

00:15:17.240 --> 00:15:20.520
Humans who can see the aura of a cursed tome.

00:15:20.740 --> 00:15:21.860
Aura?

00:15:22.560 --> 00:15:24.520
We cannot see it,

00:15:24.520 --> 00:15:30.030
but the glow of the emotions that reside in 
a cursed tome can appear as a light or flame.

00:15:30.880 --> 00:15:35.030
But I couldn't see it when he had it earlier.

00:15:35.730 --> 00:15:40.080
It may be because of the 
incident with your brother.

00:15:40.880 --> 00:15:46.140
I have heard of some who became able 
to see it after intense emotional stress.

00:15:49.100 --> 00:15:51.550
Hitaki did that because of this book?

00:15:52.420 --> 00:15:54.800
Tsugumi-sama, try to stay composed.

00:15:55.030 --> 00:15:57.780
I'm sorry, Gramps. I'll be fine.

00:15:57.780 --> 00:15:58.310
All right.

00:15:59.540 --> 00:16:00.810
Hayato?

00:16:02.560 --> 00:16:03.840
I want you!

00:16:04.660 --> 00:16:05.440
Huh?

00:16:06.940 --> 00:16:08.170
Hey, Hayato!

00:16:10.390 --> 00:16:16.200
No, I mean, I want your ability 
to see the auras... for Fukurou.

00:16:16.440 --> 00:16:17.700
Fukurou?

00:16:18.390 --> 00:16:22.800
Sorry, it's a nickname for the Imperial Library
Intelligence Asset Management Bureau.

00:16:22.800 --> 00:16:23.710
See?

00:16:26.140 --> 00:16:27.710
Please, Kuze-san.

00:16:28.390 --> 00:16:29.960
Please join as one of our colleagues.

00:16:30.280 --> 00:16:31.840
Come on, stop it, Hayato.

00:16:31.840 --> 00:16:32.900
Please!

00:16:33.340 --> 00:16:34.800
Hang on a second!

00:16:34.800 --> 00:16:35.880
Please!

00:16:45.500 --> 00:16:46.530
Nee-san!

00:16:46.760 --> 00:16:48.110
Hitaki!

00:16:48.110 --> 00:16:50.440
Help me, Nee-san!

00:16:48.970 --> 00:16:50.440
Hitaki!

00:16:54.380 --> 00:16:55.450
<i>I'm scared.</i>

00:16:56.280 --> 00:16:58.450
<i>I can't believe there are 
books that hurt people.</i>

00:16:59.100 --> 00:17:01.450
<i>Why would anyone write such things?</i>

00:17:02.660 --> 00:17:03.890
<i>It's unforgivable.</i>

00:17:11.790 --> 00:17:12.840
No.

00:17:13.830 --> 00:17:15.970
<i>I'm so unfair.</i>

00:17:16.400 --> 00:17:19.640
We believe that's what 
happened to your brother.

00:17:20.540 --> 00:17:23.170
<i>I was relieved when I heard that.</i>

00:17:23.680 --> 00:17:25.810
<i>That it might not be my fault.</i>

00:17:26.980 --> 00:17:29.150
<i>But it </i>is<i> my fault.</i>

00:17:29.490 --> 00:17:34.320
I understand. You don't really 
want to do this either, do you?

00:17:37.840 --> 00:17:41.930
<i>Hitaki was exactly right, 
but I didn't want to admit it.</i>

00:17:46.580 --> 00:17:47.830
<i>I...</i>

00:17:48.420 --> 00:17:49.960
That's not true!

00:17:49.960 --> 00:17:52.200
This is none of your business!

00:17:54.070 --> 00:17:56.220
<i>I said such a cruel thing to him.</i>

00:17:56.550 --> 00:17:59.220
<i>Something that hurt him so badly.</i>

00:18:01.380 --> 00:18:04.470
<i>If I hadn't said that, Hitaki would
have gone to town with me.</i>

00:18:04.940 --> 00:18:07.220
<i>And he wouldn't have taken out that book!</i>

00:18:10.620 --> 00:18:11.980
<i>It's my fault.</i>

00:18:12.940 --> 00:18:14.060
<i>It's my...</i>

00:18:15.740 --> 00:18:16.860
<i>It's my...</i>

00:18:19.530 --> 00:18:21.500
You mustn't blame yourself.

00:18:29.680 --> 00:18:31.630
U-Um...

00:18:32.400 --> 00:18:36.320
I'm Tokimiya Shiori of the Imperial Library
Intelligence Asset Management Bureau.

00:18:36.320 --> 00:18:38.460
Ah, there you are.

00:18:38.460 --> 00:18:41.890
I did request that you please 
wait in the reception room.

00:18:41.890 --> 00:18:43.120
Forgive me.

00:18:45.720 --> 00:18:49.300
My subordinates were rather 
rude to you last night.

00:18:49.300 --> 00:18:50.400
Not at all.

00:18:51.340 --> 00:18:54.800
How did you feel about 
the cursed tomes, Kuze-san?

00:18:56.720 --> 00:18:59.480
I have always loved books.

00:19:00.100 --> 00:19:05.490
Books can give you a taste of 
the joy, pleasure, and at times,

00:19:06.210 --> 00:19:10.480
fear and suffering in life that we wouldn't 
otherwise get to experience.

00:19:11.530 --> 00:19:16.420
But for a book... for a book 
to do something so awful...

00:19:16.660 --> 00:19:19.500
Given that your brother has
been affected in this way,

00:19:19.500 --> 00:19:23.820
I'm sure you're filled with feelings 
of hatred for the cursed tomes

00:19:23.820 --> 00:19:27.430
as well as the feeling that 
what happened was your fault.

00:19:28.580 --> 00:19:33.440
Do you believe the person who wrote the book 
your brother read should be punished?

00:19:34.580 --> 00:19:36.300
I'm not sure.

00:19:36.300 --> 00:19:42.450
I believe that we at Fukurou have a duty
to oversee what cannot be judged by laws.

00:19:43.220 --> 00:19:44.890
I would like to ask you again:

00:19:44.890 --> 00:19:48.480
Would you be willing to 
assist us with your ability?

00:19:51.160 --> 00:19:52.640
<i>Regarding your marriage,</i>

00:19:52.640 --> 00:19:55.540
<i>I've asked Mr. Yashiro to put 
it on hold for the time being.</i>

00:19:55.860 --> 00:19:57.480
<i>Father...</i>

00:19:57.480 --> 00:20:01.290
<i>I am truly glad that Hitaki 
didn't lose his life.</i>

00:20:33.590 --> 00:20:35.080
Tsugumi-sama...

00:20:37.820 --> 00:20:39.500
I've decided.

00:20:40.400 --> 00:20:44.510
I'm not doing this for some noble reason 
like using my ability to help others.

00:20:45.360 --> 00:20:48.700
I just feel like I can't continue to be this way,

00:20:48.700 --> 00:20:54.060
and I must try to change myself, 
even if only a little bit.

00:20:54.060 --> 00:20:55.520
For Hitaki's sake, too.

00:20:56.070 --> 00:20:59.100
Yes, my lady.

00:21:01.220 --> 00:21:02.650
Please take care.

00:21:03.460 --> 00:21:05.150
I'll be going now.

00:21:10.160 --> 00:21:12.660
Theater

00:21:14.650 --> 00:21:15.790
<i>Cursed tomes.</i>

00:21:16.240 --> 00:21:17.290
<i>Auras.</i>

00:21:17.670 --> 00:21:19.090
<i>And Fukurou.</i>

00:21:20.280 --> 00:21:23.550
<i>As if guided by a greatly fluctuating fate,</i>

00:21:24.470 --> 00:21:28.590
<i>the bird flies out of its cage and up to the sky.</i>

00:21:29.930 --> 00:21:34.520
<i>This is the beginning of Kuze Tsugumi's story.</i>

00:21:38.750 --> 00:21:42.030
Welcome to the Imperial Library 
Intelligence Asset Management Bureau.

00:21:42.600 --> 00:21:44.200
Thank you for having me.

00:23:20.340 --> 00:23:24.400
<i>I'm Tokimiya Shiori of the Imperial Library 
Intelligence Asset Management Bureau.</i>

00:23:21.100 --> 00:23:36.370
Chapter 2:  "The Imperial Library Intelligence 
Asset Management Bureau -Fukurou-"

00:23:24.400 --> 00:23:26.980
<i>You're finally starting 
a new life for yourself.</i>

00:23:26.980 --> 00:23:29.590
<i>On behalf of Fukurou, I welcome you.</i>

00:23:29.590 --> 00:23:32.620
<i>We have many members who 
are difficult to work with,</i>

00:23:32.620 --> 00:23:35.490
<i>but don't worry. You'll get used to it.</i>

00:23:35.490 --> 00:23:38.860
<i>Now then, I'm expecting you to 
play an active part, my lady.</i>
